cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this theory, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Lifecycle Governance Doctrine (LGD): Registry, Evidence, and Gates Across the Full Life of AI and Devices"

abstract: >-
  A governance doctrine for AI and autonomous systems. Every self-governing
  entity must be governed as a full-lifecycle chain rather than by single-point
  checks, under three laws: Registry at birth (identity, creator, governance
  ownership), Evidence for every key act (logs, risk register, change records),
  and Gates before every evolution (trigger, assessment, authorization, review —
  with humans holding sign-off). The reference model is medical-device lifecycle
  regulation, generalized across multiple regulated domains.

authors:
  - family-names: Zhao
    given-names: Xinghua
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0512-1237"

type: software

